    "text": "DE ORATIONE MOYSI, ON MEDIO QUADRAGESIME.\n\u00c6FTER \u00d0AM \u00d0E MOYSES SE M\u00c6RA HERETOGA OF \u00c6gyfta lande mid his leode ferde, and ofer\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Moyses to \u00feam cenan Iosue, Geceos \u00f0e nu w\u00e6ras, and gewend tomergen togeanes Amaleh, and\nIosue \u00fea ferde and feaht wi\u00f0 Amalech, and Moyses \u00fea astah to \u00feam sticolan munte, mid Aarone and\n\u00dea ahefde Moyses his handa on gebedum, and Iosue h\u00e6fde sige and sloh \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan.\nEft \u00f0onne Moyses ne mihte lencg habban his handa astrehte, \u00feonne h\u00e6fde Amalech sige \u00fea hwile and\nSwa oft swa Moyses ahefde his handa on gebedum, swa h\u00e6fde Iosue heofonlicne fultum; and sona swa\nMoyses handa w\u00e6ron mycclum gehefegode, Aaron \u00fea alede \u00e6nne ormetne stan under Moysen, and he\nIosue \u00fea h\u00e6fde heofonlicne fultum, and afligde Amalech and his folc mid w\u00e6pnum.\nBe \u00feisum we magon tocnawen \u00fe\u00e6t we Cristene sceolan on \u00e6lcere earfo\u00f0nisse \u00e6fre to Gode clypian and\nMoyses h\u00e6fde sige and mycelne fultum, \u00fea hwile \u00fee he heold his handa on gebedum, and his willa ne\nNu habbe we gewinn wi\u00f0 \u00feone hetelan deofol, and he win\u00f0 on us for\u00f0an \u00fee he w\u00e6lhreow is.\nHu bi\u00f0 \u00feonne gif we nella\u00f0 to \u00feam H\u00e6lende clypian, \u00feonne Moyses werignyss ne mihte beon beladod?\nWitodlice bi\u00f0 oferswi\u00f0ed \u00feurh \u00feone swicolan deofol, se\u00f0e nele clypian Crist him to fultume.\n\u00c6lc rihtwis man h\u00e6fde, swa swa we r\u00e6da\u00f0 on bocum, fultum and hreddinge, se\u00f0e mid fullum geleafan\nNis nan \u00feincg swa la\u00f0 \u00feam geleafleasum deofle swa \u00fe\u00e6t hine man gebidde bealdlice to Gode, for\u00f0an \u00fee\nFor\u00fei he cunna\u00f0 georne \u00feonne we clypia\u00f0 to Gode, hu he m\u00e6ge tobr\u00e6can \u00fea gebedu mid costnungum,\n\u00deonne we us gebidda\u00f0 mid bylewitum mode, \u00feonne sprece we so\u00f0lice to Gode sylfum swa, and \u00feonne\nSe man mot hine gebiddan swa swa he m\u00e6g and cann, for\u00f0an \u00fee se \u00e6lmihtiga God cann \u00e6lc gereord\nMan sceal swa\u00feeah secan cyrcan gelome, and man ne mot spellian ne spr\u00e6ce drifan binnan Godes\nNe man ne sceal drincan o\u00f0\u00f0e dwollice etan binnan Godes huse, \u00fee is gehalgod to \u00feam \u00fe\u00e6t man Godes\nNu do\u00f0 menn swa\u00feeah dyslice foroft, \u00fe\u00e6t hi willa\u00f0 wacian and wodlice drincan binnan godes huse and\nSe\u00fee wylle wacian and wur\u00f0ian Godes halgan, wacie mid stilnysse and ne wyrcan nan gehlyd, ac singe\nUs is neod \u00fe\u00e6t we clypian to Criste gelome, buton hygeleaste and hiwunge swa \u00f0eah.\nSwa swa se lichoma leofa\u00f0 be hlafe and drence, swa sceal seo sawl libban be lare and gebedum.\nFela dyslice d\u00e6da deria\u00f0 mancynne, o\u00f0\u00f0e for anwylnysse o\u00f0\u00f0e for ungerade.\nSwa swa sume menn do\u00f0 \u00fee dyslice f\u00e6sta\u00f0 ofer heora mihte on gem\u00e6nelicum lenctene, swa swa we\nSume f\u00e6ston eac swa, \u00fe\u00e6t hi forsawon to etanne buton on \u00f0one o\u00f0erne d\u00e6g, and \u00e6ton \u00feonne\nNu gesetton \u00f0a halgan f\u00e6deras \u00fe\u00e6t we f\u00e6ston mid gerade, and \u00e6lce d\u00e6g eton mid gedafenlicnysse\n\u00dees eard nis eac ealles swa m\u00e6genf\u00e6st, her on uteweardan \u00fe\u00e6re eor\u00f0an bradnysse, swa swa heo is\nNe nu nis mancynn swa mihtig swa menn w\u00e6ron \u00e6t fruman.\nNis nan f\u00e6sten swa god ne Gode swa gecweme, swa swa \u00fe\u00e6t f\u00e6sten is \u00fe\u00e6t man fulnysse onscunige,\nNe sceal se wise mann beon butan godum weorcum, ne se ealde ne beo buton \u00e6wf\u00e6stnysse, ne se\nEft bi\u00f0 swi\u00f0e \u00fewyrlic, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0earfa beo modig, and forcu\u00f0lic hit bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t cyning beo unrihtwis.\nEac bi\u00f0 swy\u00fee derigendlic \u00fe\u00e6t bisceop beo gymeleas, and unfremful bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t folc beo butan steora,\n\u00deissere worulde h\u00e6l is \u00fe\u00e6t heo witan h\u00e6bbe, and swa ma witena beo\u00f0 on bradnysse middaneardes,\nNe bi\u00f0 se na wita \u00fee unwislice leofa\u00f0, ac bi\u00f0 open sott \u00feeah \u00fee him swa ne \u00f0ince.\nGif \u00f0a gehadodan menn healda\u00f0 Godes \u00f0eowdom on gesettan timan, and syferlice libba\u00f0, and gif \u00f0a\nGif \u00f0onne \u00fea heafodmenn and \u00f0a gehadodan lareowas \u00feyses ne gyma\u00f0, ac \u00feenca\u00f0 embe woruld\u00feincg,\nWel we magon ge\u00f0encan hu wel hit ferde mid us, \u00fea\u00f0a \u00feis igland w\u00e6s wunigende on sibbe, and\nHu w\u00e6s hit \u00f0a si\u00f0\u00f0an \u00f0a \u00fea man towearp munuclif, and Godes biggengas to bysmore h\u00e6fde, buton\nBe \u00feysum cw\u00e6\u00f0 se \u00e6lmihtiga God to Moyse on \u00feam w\u00e6stene, Gif ge on minum bebodum fara\u00f0, and\nGif ge \u00feonne me forseo\u00f0 and mine gesetnyssa awurpa\u00f0, ic eac swy\u00f0e hr\u00e6dlice on eow hit gewrece; ic\n\u00deonne swince ge on idel, gif ge sawa\u00f0 eower land \u00f0onne seo eor\u00f0e ne spryt eow n\u00e6nne w\u00e6stm; and\nIc asende eac yrh\u00f0e into eowrum heortum, \u00fe\u00e6t eower nan ne dear eowrum feondum wi\u00f0standan.\n\u00deus spr\u00e6c God gefyrn be \u00feam folce Israhel; hit is swa \u00f0eah swa gedon swy\u00f0e neah mid us, nu on\nWe sceolan God wur\u00f0ian mid so\u00f0re anr\u00e6dnysse, for\u00f0an \u00fee he is \u00e6lmihtig God, and he us to menn\nGod gewr\u00e6c fram frym\u00f0e mid witum his forsewennysse, \u00e6rest on \u00f0am \u00e6nglum \u00fee unr\u00e6dlice\nEft \u00f0a \u00fea God wolde wrecan mid fyre \u00fea fulan forligeras \u00fe\u00e6s fracodostan mennisces, Sodomitiscra\nHabraham \u00fea b\u00e6d \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan \u00f0us, \u00feu Drihten, \u00fee demst eallum deadlicum fl\u00e6sce, ne scealt \u00f0u\nGif \u00f0\u00e6r beo\u00f0 fiftig wera wunigende on \u00feam earde, rihtwise \u00e6tforan \u00f0e, ara him eallum.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 God him to eft, Ic arige him eallum gif ic \u00f0\u00e6r finde fiftig rihtwisra.\n\u00dea began Abraham eft biddan God georne, \u00fe\u00e6t he hi ne fordyde gif \u00f0\u00e6r feowertig w\u00e6ron rihtwisra\nGod him \u00f0\u00e6s ti\u00feode, and he began git biddan o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t he becom to tyn mannum, and him ti\u00f0ode God \u00f0a,\nGod sende \u00f0a sona to \u00f0am sceandlicum mannum twegen englas on \u00e6fen, and hi Abrahames bro\u00f0or\nGod sende \u00f0a fyr on merigen and fulne swefel him to, and forb\u00e6rnde hi ealle and heora burga\nBe \u00f0ysum man m\u00e6g tocnawan \u00fe\u00e6t micclum fremia\u00f0 \u00feam l\u00e6wedum mannum \u00fea gel\u00e6redan Godes\nEalswa Dathan and Abiron \u00f0e dyslice spr\u00e6con, and mycelne teonan Moyse gedydon ongean Godes\nGod him wear\u00f0 \u00fea yrre, and seo eor\u00fee tob\u00e6rst \u00fe\u00e6r\u00f0\u00e6r hi wicodon, mid wifum and mid cyldum on\nManega of \u00f0am folce myslice oft ceorodon, and fandoden Godes and gremedon mid spr\u00e6con, ac God\nAnd Gode is swy\u00f0e la\u00f0 on geleaffullum folce, \u00fe\u00e6t hi beon unge\u00f0w\u00e6re and \u00fewyre him betwynan; and\nEft Dauid se cyning \u00f0eah \u00fee he gecweme were Gode, agylte swy\u00f0e \u00feearle, and God him sende \u00f0a to\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Dauid him to, Unea\u00f0e me is \u00f0is, ac me is swa \u00f0eah leofre \u00fe\u00e6t ic on Godes handa befealle\nGod sende \u00f0a sona sumne encgel him to, and se encgel ofsloh hundseofontig \u00f0usenda on Dauides\n\u00dea com se encgel \u00fe\u00e6r se cynincg sylf w\u00e6s, and wolde \u00f0a slean \u00fea ceastergewaran.\nAc Gode ofhreow \u00f0a and hra\u00f0e cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00f0am engle, genoh genoh hit is nu, heald \u00feine handa.\n\u00dea geseah Dauid sylf hu se encgel sloh \u00fe\u00e6t folc, and clypode to Gode, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 mid angsumnysse, Ic\nIc bidde \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu awende wi\u00f0 min \u00feine hand, and wi\u00f0 minne hired \u00feine hatheortnysse.\n\u00dea com Gad se witega gangende, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 him to , Far nu and ar\u00e6r hra\u00f0e an weofod Gode, and\n\u00dea dyde Dauid swa, and Drihten him gemiltsode and se encgel ne moste \u00fea menn ofslean leng.\nGod nolde ofslean \u00feone scyldigan Dauid, \u00feeah\u00f0e he syngode, for\u00f0an \u00fee he swy\u00f0e oft dyde ge \u00e6r ge\nEft w\u00e6s sum leodscipe \u00fee se lifigenda God wolde gewitnian for heora gewitleasum d\u00e6dum; \u00fe\u00e6t\n\u00dea sende God him to sumne witegan, Ionas gehaten, and het hi geswican o\u00f0\u00f0e hi ealle sceoldon\nSe cynincg \u00f0a gecyrde sona mid his leode, and hi ealle f\u00e6ston \u00f0ry dagas on an, and Drihten him\nNe m\u00e6g nan mann awritan ne mid wordum areccan hu oft se \u00e6lmihtiga god egeslice gewr\u00e6c his\nWe ne sceolan ceorigan ne sorhlice bem\u00e6nan \u00feeah \u00f0e us ungelimp on \u00e6htum getime, for\u00f0an \u00fee seo\nFela ungelimpa beo\u00f0 on ende \u00f0issere worulde, ac gehwa mot forberan emlice his d\u00e6l, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0urh\n\u00dees tima is endenext and ende \u00feyssere worulde, and menn beo\u00f0 geworhte wolice him betwynan, swa\n\u00deonne \u00f0inc\u00f0 \u00feam arleasum swylce hi \u00e6fre motan libban, and ne cunnon \u00f0one cwyde \u00fee God cw\u00e6\u00f0 be\n\u00d0a synd blodige weras \u00f0e wyrca\u00f0 manslihtas, and \u00f0a\u00f0e manna sawla beswica\u00f0 to forwyrde.\n\u00d0a sceolan geendian swy\u00f0e yfelum dea\u00f0e, gif hi \u00e6r geendunge heora yfel ne gebeta\u00f0.\nAnd \u00f0eah \u00fee hi sume lybbon leng \u00f0onne hi sceoldon, for Godes ge\u00f0ylde \u00fe\u00e6t him ne frema\u00f0 naht, ac hi\nGodes wisdom clypa\u00f0, and cwy\u00f0 to eallum mannum mid f\u00e6derlicre lufe \u00feus f\u00e6gere tihtende, Min\nHafa \u00fee truwa on God of ealre \u00f0inre heortan, and ne truwa \u00f0u na swy\u00f0e on \u00feinre snoternysse.\n\u00deenc \u00e6fre embe God on eallum \u00f0inum wegum, and he sylf gewissa\u00f0 wel \u00feine fare.\nEadig bi\u00f0 se man se\u00f0e gemet wisdom, for\u00f0an \u00fee se wisdom is selra \u00feone scinende gold, and he ana is\n\u00de\u00e6t is se wisdom, \u00fe\u00e6t man wislice libbe, and his d\u00e6da gefadige to his Drihtnes willan, \u00fe\u00e6t he edlean",
